      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 2.1,
          "en": "So at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 5.13,
          "en": "we've seen in detail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.13,
          "end": 6.87,
          "en": "how we can manage caching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.87,
          "end": 10.65,
          "en": "when sending requests to external APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.65,
          "end": 12.81,
          "en": "But of course, in the previous sections,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.81,
          "end": 14.76,
          "en": "we also learned that often",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.76,
          "end": 16.56,
          "en": "you might not need to communicate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.56,
          "end": 18,
          "en": "with external APIs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 18,
          "end": 20.98,
          "en": "You might not be using this fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 21.87,
          "end": 24.09,
          "en": "and therefore, in this and the next lectures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.09,
          "end": 27.51,
          "en": "I'll show you how you can still take advantage of caching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.51,
          "end": 31.23,
          "en": "and control caching when using another data source",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.23,
          "end": 34.29,
          "en": "like a database to which you directly reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.29,
          "end": 36.543,
          "en": "from inside your next application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.41,
          "end": 38.79,
          "en": "Therefore, to get started,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.79,
          "end": 42.31,
          "en": "I'll comment out this code where I sent this fetch request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.26,
          "end": 48.26,
          "en": "and instead, I will call getMessages here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.42,
          "end": 50.1,
          "en": "in my MessagesPage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.1,
          "end": 53.82,
          "en": "and getMessages is a function from the lib folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.82,
          "end": 56.91,
          "en": "So this folder and this file in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.91,
          "end": 61.17,
          "en": "And in there, I'm managing a simple SQLite database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.17,
          "end": 63.24,
          "en": "I got a function for inserting messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.24,
          "end": 67.56,
          "en": "and I got a function for getting data from the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.56,
          "end": 71.01,
          "en": "And these are indeed synchronous functions right now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.01,
          "end": 73.56,
          "en": "because this better-sqlite free package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.56,
          "end": 76.47,
          "en": "which I'm using for interacting with the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.47,
          "end": 78.9,
          "en": "indeed does not need promises,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.9,
          "end": 81.09,
          "en": "does not need asynchronous code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.09,
          "end": 83.4,
          "en": "and therefore there is no async here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.4,
          "end": 86.58,
          "en": "And hence, we actually also don't have to await this here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.58,
          "end": 88.38,
          "en": "We can even remove async here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 88.38,
          "end": 90.663,
          "en": "if we want to on this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 92.52000000000001,
          "end": 94.71000000000001,
          "en": "So with that, we'll then get our messages here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.71000000000001,
          "end": 98.49000000000001,
          "en": "which we can output and I can do the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 98.49000000000001,
          "end": 99.75,
          "en": "in my layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 99.75,
          "end": 104.61,
          "en": "There, I also no longer wanna fetch my messages like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 104.61,
          "end": 107.4,
          "en": "Instead, we can remove async here as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.4,
          "end": 111.53999999999999,
          "en": "and get the messages by calling getMessages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.53999999999999,
          "end": 114.423,
          "en": "which is that same function from the lib folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.72999999999999,
          "end": 117.57,
          "en": "Now with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.57,
          "end": 121.11,
          "en": "if I saved it and reload, I got no messages right now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.11,
          "end": 124.47,
          "en": "but that's why I have this addMessage function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.47,
          "end": 127.08,
          "en": "And I now want to call this function again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.08,
          "end": 131.28,
          "en": "from inside this server action in the NewMessages page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.28,
          "end": 133.38,
          "en": "and pass the message that has been entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.38,
          "end": 135.12,
          "en": "by the user to addMessage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.12,
          "end": 136.893,
          "en": "And that should add a new message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.71,
          "end": 142.62,
          "en": "And therefore, with this re-added to the code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 142.62,
          "end": 146.25,
          "en": "if I go here and add a new message like test,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 146.25,
          "end": 148.26,
          "en": "it shows up on that messages page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.26,
          "end": 151.53300000000002,
          "en": "If I add test two, that also shows up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.91,
          "end": 154.44,
          "en": "And the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.44,
          "end": 158.01,
          "en": "that these messages show up here proves",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.01,
          "end": 162.09,
          "en": "that there seems to be no caching going on here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.09,
          "end": 164.28,
          "en": "though that's not entirely true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 164.28,
          "end": 168.63,
          "en": "If you recall, once we start building this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.63,
          "end": 171.24,
          "en": "for production by npm run build,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.24,
          "end": 174.78,
          "en": "we do get that page pre-rendering again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 174.78,
          "end": 178.35,
          "en": "and we get that full route cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 178.35,
          "end": 181.8,
          "en": "unless you set one of these settings here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.8,
          "end": 185.16,
          "en": "and force this page to be dynamic, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.16,
          "end": 187.62,
          "en": "But otherwise, we get this full route cache",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.62,
          "end": 190.41,
          "en": "and therefore, when building this for production,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 190.41,
          "end": 194.49,
          "en": "we indeed have the problem that we see any messages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 194.49,
          "end": 197.16,
          "en": "any data that existed at build time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 197.16,
          "end": 199.5,
          "en": "but if we add a new message thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 199.5,
          "end": 201.573,
          "en": "that indeed does now not show up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.44,
          "end": 204.57,
          "en": "So we do have some caching here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 204.57,
          "end": 206.91,
          "en": "we have that full route cache,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 206.91,
          "end": 209.31,
          "en": "but we don't have that data cache.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.31,
          "end": 213.18,
          "en": "We don't have the request deduplication",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.18,
          "end": 216.063,
          "en": "when using our own custom data source.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 216.96,
          "end": 219.11,
          "en": "Now we'll fix that problem here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 219.11,
          "end": 221.52,
          "en": "of the updated data not appearing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 221.52,
          "end": 223.89,
          "en": "due to the full route cache later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 223.89,
          "end": 226.95,
          "en": "For now, I'll go back to my development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 226.95,
          "end": 230.49,
          "en": "and I'll focus on the request deduplication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 230.49,
          "end": 232.983,
          "en": "And on that full route cache first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 233.91,
          "end": 236.673,
          "en": "We can also stop that backend server here, by the way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 237.84,
          "end": 241.05,
          "en": "So my Next.js development server is running again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 241.05,
          "end": 242.19,
          "en": "and that indeed means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 242.19,
          "end": 243.78,
          "en": "that with the development server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 243.78,
          "end": 245.79,
          "en": "we see all the updated data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 245.79,
          "end": 248.313,
          "en": "because we don't have that full route cache here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 249.36,
          "end": 252.93,
          "en": "But it also means if we take a look at the logs here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 252.93,
          "end": 256.17,
          "en": "that we actually hit the database every time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 256.17,
          "end": 258.06,
          "en": "I reload this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 258.06,
          "end": 260.76,
          "en": "and we indeed always hit it twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 260.76,
          "end": 263.4,
          "en": "because I'm fetching the same messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 263.4,
          "end": 266.76,
          "en": "both from inside the page and the layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 266.76,
          "end": 269.49,
          "en": "It's the same request which triggers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 269.49,
          "end": 271.74,
          "en": "the same SQL command here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 271.74,
          "end": 273,
          "en": "the same query,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 273,
          "end": 275.58,
          "en": "but we run this twice because we send it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 275.58,
          "end": 276.87,
          "en": "in two different places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 276.87,
          "end": 280.53,
          "en": "We got no request deduplication going on here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 280.53,
          "end": 282.65999999999997,
          "en": "because we're not using the fetch function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 282.65999999999997,
          "end": 284.04,
          "en": "and out of the box,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 284.04,
          "end": 287.733,
          "en": "Next.js only supports that for the next function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 288.87,
          "end": 292.26,
          "en": "But we can make this request deduplication work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 292.26,
          "end": 294.33,
          "en": "for our own data fetching code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 294.33,
          "end": 296.64,
          "en": "that uses our own data source",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 296.64,
          "end": 298.38,
          "en": "with help of another function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 298.38,
          "end": 300.96,
          "en": "that can be imported from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 300.96,
          "end": 305.04,
          "en": "So not from Next, but from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 305.04,
          "end": 306.96,
          "en": "And from that React library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 306.96,
          "end": 309.843,
          "en": "we can import a cache function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 312.15,
          "end": 315.66,
          "en": "Now, this cache function is meant to be wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 315.66,
          "end": 317.76,
          "en": "around one of your functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 317.76,
          "end": 322.5,
          "en": "for which request deduplication should then occur.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 322.5,
          "end": 325.47,
          "en": "And you can easily use that cache function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 325.47,
          "end": 329.58,
          "en": "by wrapping it around getMessages, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 329.58,
          "end": 331.2,
          "en": "Now, this is now not valid code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 331.2,
          "end": 333.57,
          "en": "So what we should do here is we should create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 333.57,
          "end": 335.79,
          "en": "a new constant call getMessages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 335.79,
          "end": 338.52,
          "en": "and set that equal to that cached function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 338.52,
          "end": 339.933,
          "en": "and that's now valid again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 341.58,
          "end": 343.23,
          "en": "Now, if you do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 343.23,
          "end": 348.03,
          "en": "and you reload this page, everything works as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 348.03,
          "end": 352.53,
          "en": "But what you'll notice is that now, if I clear that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 352.53,
          "end": 355.023,
          "en": "and rerun my development server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 356.4,
          "end": 358.86,
          "en": "if I reload this messages page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 358.86,
          "end": 362.103,
          "en": "there is just one request to the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 363.81,
          "end": 368.16,
          "en": "Now we see that one request for every reload I perform,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 368.16,
          "end": 372.36,
          "en": "but it's just one request per page reload instead of two,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 372.36,
          "end": 374.13,
          "en": "because this cache function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 374.13,
          "end": 375.81,
          "en": "which is provided by React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 375.81,
          "end": 378.291,
          "en": "when wrapped around one of our functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 378.291,
          "end": 381.63,
          "en": "indeed make sure that under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 381.63,
          "end": 384.24,
          "en": "React cache is the data returned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 384.24,
          "end": 386.82,
          "en": "by that function when it's called the first time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 386.82,
          "end": 388.53,
          "en": "anywhere in our application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 388.53,
          "end": 391.5,
          "en": "inside of one single request cycle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 391.5,
          "end": 393.12,
          "en": "And then the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 393.12,
          "end": 396.42,
          "en": "by that function is reused in all the places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
